<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43688" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sentus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>thorny</i>, <i>rough</i>, <i>rugged</i> (<b>poet.</b> and very rare): loca senta situ,
			* <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 6, 462</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 4,
				436</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vepres,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. in Symm. 2, 1039</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rubus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Apoth. 123</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">video sentum, squalidum, aegrum, pannis
					annisque obsitum (hominem),</span>”
				<i>bristly</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Eun. 2, 2, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
